Opening a lightcone structure collection (halo/galaxy properties plus particles across many redshift steps) now resolves parent-child links per step instead of concatenating all link metadata across every step first. This avoids the large memory spike (and OOM kills) that previously occurred when opening multi-step lightcone structure collections; peak memory now scales roughly per-step rather than with the sum over all steps. Sorted-write round-trips are also fixed: linked datasets are re-sorted per step so a sorted lightcone structure collection can be written and reopened without corrupting per-step link offsets.
